course: dictionary
lesson: 1100
title: Brainy and friends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Some birds are brainy: a crow drops walnuts on a road for cars to crack, a jay remembers where it buried thousands of acorns, and an African grey parrot can name colours.» The examples show what brainy means: solving problems, remembering things and learning. Brainy can describe animals as well as people.
explain: Brainy is informal, so you hear it in chatty, everyday talk more than in formal writing. It means very clever and good at thinking and learning, or smart in a bookish way. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «a clever crow» still makes sense.
explain: Brainy can be friendly or teasing. A brainbox (UK) or brainiac (US) is a very brainy person. In stories the brainy friend often solves the puzzle, but some people feel teased when called brainy, so use it kindly.
fact: Brainy means very clever and good at thinking and learning.
fact: Brainy is informal: you say it in everyday talk, not in formal writing.
fact: Brainbox (UK) and brainiac (US) both mean a very brainy person.
fact: The forms are brainy, brainier and brainiest, as in «brainier than his brother».
fact: Some people feel teased when called brainy, so use it kindly.
exercise: «Some birds are brainy: a crow drops walnuts on a road for cars to crack.» What does brainy mean in this sentence? | Able to fly very fast | Good at singing | *Very clever at solving problems | Covered in soft feathers
exercise: Mia says her friend is a brainbox. What does she mean? | Her friend has a very big head | Her friend is always tired | *Her friend is very clever | Her friend lives in a box
exercise: Tom is brainier than his brother. What does brainier mean? | *Cleverer | Taller | Hungrier | Quieter
test: «A jay remembers where it buried thousands of acorns.» What does this sentence show about jays? | Jays hate acorns | *Jays are good at remembering | Jays cannot see well | Jays only eat in winter
test: Why should you use the word brainy kindly? | Because it is a very long word | *Some children feel teased when called brainy | Because it only means tall | Because it is a formal word used in exams
exam: Ellie says brainy is a formal word used in school reports. Is she right? | No, it means quiet and calm | Yes, it is only used in formal writing | Yes, it means tall and strong | *No, it is informal and used in everyday talk
